  "decision_conditions": [
    "Occupier",
    "The development must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date hereof.\r\rReason: To comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended.",
    "All external facing materials, treatments and finishes shall be similar to those of the original building and maintained and retained thereafter. This applies unless differences are shown on the drawings we have approved. \r\rReason: To ensure that the extension harmonises with the existing building and to ensure compliance with Policy 28 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "The development must be carried out in accordance with the provisions of the Fire Safety Strategy Reasonable Exception Statement - Kingdom Hall, Queens Road, SM6 0AG, dated 3rd September 2025 and submitted with the application. \r\rReason: To ensure that the development incorporates the necessary fire safety measures in accordance with the Mayor's London Plan Policy D12.",
    "The plant shall only be operational between the hours of 0800hrs and 2200hrs as outlined in Table 2 of the Acoustic Assessment of Proposed New Mechanical Services Equipment Report Reference: 250115-R001B.\r\rReason: To safeguard the amenity of the neighbours by minimising impacts of the development that would otherwise give rise to nuisance in accordance with Policies 29 and 34 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.\r"
  ],
